<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    UNREFERENCED as of the onboarding-wide Compose migration (ROADMAP.md §5.26 — see this
    commit's entry): CoreDataConsentFragment now hosts a Compose screen (CoreDataConsentScreen, in
    ui/onboarding/) via a single ComposeView instead of inflating this file. Left in place
    deliberately rather than deleted in the same pass — cleanup of now-dead XML layouts left
    behind by the Compose migration is being tracked as its own step (see
    fragment_first_mission_scheduling.xml, marked the same way in the prior Compose-migration
    PR), so other screens' still-live layouts and this file's history stay easy to diff
    against each other rather than being interleaved with unrelated deletions. Do not re-wire
    this file back in without updating CoreDataConsentFragment.kt's kdoc, which documents the Compose
    migration as the current source of truth for this screen.

    Original content below preserved as-is, for reference only — kept in sync with neither the
    Fragment nor strings.xml going forward.
-->

<!--
    Onboarding, Consent & Interaction Spec §2.6 (Core Data Consent) — real content, replacing
    OnboardingPlaceholderFragment at the coreDataConsentFragment destination.

    §2.6's two content requirements, one paragraph each: (1) standard local-storage/Mission-
    enforcement consent, framed as required-not-optional since this is core function rather
    than an optional data use (Architecture doc §3.1's "Mission enforcement must work fully
    offline" is the concrete claim this paragraph makes to the user); (2) plain-language
    local-first + optional cloud-sync explanation (same §3.1 citation). A third, shorter
    paragraph states the local "delete your data" affordance mentioned in Architecture doc
    §3.2's rescoped-for-personal-use section — not a formal export/deletion regime, just the
    plain fact that a full local wipe exists if someone wants to walk away.

    Deliberately NOT this screen's job (see CoreDataConsentFragment's kdoc for the full
    reasoning): Unsupervised Reliability consent. PRD §13.4 is an explicit hard rule against
    bundling that into this screen — it stays its own destination
    (unsupervisedReliabilityOptInFragment), the next one in the graph.

    Required, not optional (§2.6's own framing, echoed in the nav-graph comment above this
    destination) — so unlike unsupervisedReliabilityOptInFragment's eventual "decline"-shaped
    control, this screen has exactly one forward action: acknowledge and continue. There is no
    decline path because there is nothing to decline into; the app's core function (Mission
    enforcement) cannot run without this consent, matching Architecture doc §3.1's own framing
    of local storage as the source of truth, not an optional add-on.
-->
<ScrollView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent">

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        android:padding="24dp">

        <TextView
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:textSize="14sp"
            android:textColor="@android:color/darker_gray"
            android:text="@string/core_data_consent_step_progress" />

        <TextView
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="12dp"
            android:layout_marginBottom="20dp"
            android:textSize="24sp"
            android:textStyle="bold"
            android:text="@string/core_data_consent_title" />

        <TextView
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginBottom="16dp"
            android:textSize="15sp"
            android:text="@string/core_data_consent_required_body" />

        <TextView
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginBottom="16dp"
            android:textSize="15sp"
            android:text="@string/core_data_consent_local_first_body" />

        <TextView
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginBottom="28dp"
            android:textSize="15sp"
            android:text="@string/core_data_consent_delete_body" />

        <Button
            android:id="@+id/coreDataConsentBackButton"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginBottom="12dp"
            android:text="@string/onboarding_placeholder_back" />

        <Button
            android:id="@+id/coreDataConsentContinueButton"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:text="@string/core_data_consent_continue" />

    </LinearLayout>

</ScrollView>
